WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.650
Stage nineteen: the home trainer, sized to you.

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:12.235
It's raining: Camille will ride seventy minutes at home, in zone two. But how many watts is zone two?

3
00:00:12.335 --> 00:00:21.972
The coach works it out from her own FIT files: power against heart rate, ride after ride. About a hundred and forty watts. An estimate, not a test.

4
00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:30.987
A hundred and sixteen MyWhoosh routes, fetched once with her account: distance, climbing, difficulty, loop or point to point.

5
00:00:31.087 --> 00:00:34.985
The password is typed in a terminal. Never in the chat.

6
00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:40.736
The model works out each route's time at her power, with her weight and the bike's.

7
00:00:40.836 --> 00:00:49.086
Too short, too long, too steep for an endurance ride: out. Limmat Loop, two laps: one hour ten, give or take ten percent.

8
00:00:49.936 --> 00:00:54.218
The route goes to the watch, in the workout name, and into the week.

9
00:00:54.318 --> 00:01:00.776
The target stays heart rate. If it climbs, ease off the watts, even if the lap goes unfinished.

10
00:01:01.626 --> 00:01:09.833
Add it to the MyWhoosh calendar too? The coach offers, shows what it will write, and waits for a yes. Never in automatic mode.

11
00:01:10.683 --> 00:01:18.122
In the Gear view, the Home trainer card: the declared equipment, the watts per zone, and the latest rides with power.

12
00:01:18.222 --> 00:01:21.374
All of it stays off until you switch it on.

13
00:01:23.924 --> 00:01:28.398
To go further: the “MyWhoosh routes” page of the documentation.
